**`auto-memory-hook.mjs:JsonFileBackend.store()` — line 59**

Every single `store(entry)` call serializes the entire `entries` Map and writes the full JSON file to disk. During a bulk import this can mean hundreds of sequential full-file writes.

```javascript
// CURRENT — auto-memory-hook.mjs:59
async store(entry) { this.entries.set(entry.id, entry); this._persist(); }
// _persist() writes JSON.stringify([...this.entries.values()], null, 2) every time
```

**Fix**: Debounce or batch writes; flush only at the end of bulk operations:

```javascript
_scheduleFlush() {
  if (this._flushTimer) return;
  this._flushTimer = setTimeout(() => {
    this._flushTimer = null;
    this._persist();
  }, 100); // coalesce writes within 100ms
}

async store(entry) {
  this.entries.set(entry.id, entry);
  this._scheduleFlush();
}

async bulkInsert(entries) {
  for (const e of entries) this.entries.set(e.id, e);
  this._persist(); // single write for the whole batch
}
```

